meta {
  name: Credit Notifications - Get
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/billing/credit-notifications
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
}

docs {
  The workspace's credit notification preferences — when it wants to be
  warned about credit spend. Requires the `billing.view` permission.

  - `out_of_credits_enabled` — whether the workspace is told when it runs out
    of credits (or reaches its overage cap). On by default.
  - `thresholds` — percentages of the period's allowance that trigger a
    "running low" notification. These are what is actually enforced, so this
    holds the defaults where the workspace never chose its own.
  - `is_default` — whether `thresholds` are the estate defaults rather than
    the workspace's own choice.
  - `default_thresholds` / `maximum_thresholds` — what a reset would restore,
    and how many thresholds may be configured.

  These are workspace-wide switches over *whether* a warning is sent. Each
  user's choice of how to receive it stays on `/notifications/preferences`.

  Response is wrapped:
  `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { credit_notifications } }`.
}
